================================================================================
 5. SYSTEM RELIABILITY & FAULT TOLERANCE
================================================================================

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  Scenario                        │  Behavior                              │
  ├───────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  Wi-Fi Disconnected              │  LEDs still update locally. Web API    │
  │                                  │  unavailable. Blynk reconnects auto.   │
  │  Blynk Server Down               │  Local REST API + LEDs unaffected.     │
  │                                  │  Cloud dashboard offline.              │
  │  Web UI Browser Closed           │  No impact. ESP32 continues all ops.   │
  │  Unreal Engine Closed            │  No impact. All other outputs active.  │
  │  Sensor Disconnected             │  ADC reads ~0 → RED: No Voltage state. │
  │  Power Loss                      │  Full restart required (~5–10 s).      │
  │  Multiple API Clients            │  4–8 concurrent supported. Beyond      │
  │                                  │  limit, connections queued/dropped.    │
  └───────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────┘

================================================================================
 6. PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION NOTES
================================================================================

  [OPT-001] ADC Averaging: Consider multi-sample averaging (e.g., 10 reads per
            channel) to reduce noise. Adds ~100 µs per channel but improves
            measurement stability by ~60%.

  [OPT-002] JSON Buffer: Pre-allocate a fixed char buffer (~256 bytes) instead
            of Arduino String concatenation to avoid heap fragmentation.

  [OPT-003] CORS Headers: Add Access-Control-Allow-Origin to handleAPI() to
            allow cross-origin requests from the Web UI without proxy.

  [OPT-004] UE Polling: Use WebSocket upgrade instead of HTTP polling to reduce
            latency from ~1–5 s to ~50–100 ms for real-time 3D updates.

  [OPT-005] OTA Updates: Enable ArduinoOTA for wireless firmware updates,
            eliminating the need for USB connection during development.

  [OPT-006] Deep Sleep: If battery-powered, implement ESP32 deep sleep between
            measurement cycles to reduce average power to ~10 µA.

